<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#sarissa">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarissa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The sarissa was a very long pike, several metres in length, carried by the infantry of the Macedonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a>. Introduced under Philip II, it allowed several ranks of soldiers to present their points to the enemy at once. It was central to the conquests of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a> and remained the core weapon of Hellenistic armies such as that of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>.</p></div>
